From 6e3271041f3a61c456e54a45204914f40089a107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:54:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the CMS POA exempt list everywhere POA is keyed, coded,
 audited or graded

Nothing in the app knew which ICD-10-CM codes CMS exempts from POA
reporting: trainers checked the list and picked E by hand, and coders
did the same. The code-set loader now loads the FY exempt list (38,399
codes for FY2027) and stamps each code; NULL means not loaded, and then
nothing changes.

An exempt code's POA is set to E and greyed on the coder form, the key
editor, the auditor's add and claim rows and the authored-error editor.
Keys are stored with E on exempt codes on upload and edit, and existing
keys are corrected once when the list loads. POA on an exempt code is
never graded, and the auditor generator never plants a POA error on one:
on an exempt code keyed Y it planted 'N, should be Y', wrong twice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GAgNTxNNybv6W7GXL33G6z
